{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-49193" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is ${\\int }_{2}^{4}(x+1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x$ expressed as the limit of a right Riemann sum?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980754/state.json" "file_sha256" "17741a48634f24a036a10a6073a4e7584393df9153aec4e24c76bab9abdef2ae"} {"question" "q-49193" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The definite integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a right Riemann sum as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}f({x}_{m})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{m}=a+mΔx$ and $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$\n\nIn the definite integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{2}^{4}(x+1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nthe function is $f(x)=(x+1)^{2},$ the lower bound is $a=2$ and the upper bound is $b=4.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{4-2}{n}=\\frac{2}{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{4}(x+1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}f({x}_{m})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}[f(2+m\\cdot \\frac{2}{n})\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}[f(2+\\frac{2m}{n})\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}[{((2+\\frac{2m}{n})+1)}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}[{(3+\\frac{2m}{n})}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980754/state.json" "file_sha256" "17741a48634f24a036a10a6073a4e7584393df9153aec4e24c76bab9abdef2ae"} {"question" "q-49193" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980754/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "523f6f22ecb91e692fe46e7c5d5718162102afd70c6795be6f1a322c4f43120e"} {"question" "q-49193" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980754/state.json" "file_sha256" "17741a48634f24a036a10a6073a4e7584393df9153aec4e24c76bab9abdef2ae"} {"question" "q-49193" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}[{(2+\\frac{2m}{n})}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}]"] ["math" "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}[{(2+\\frac{m}{n})}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}]"] ["math" "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}[{(3+\\frac{2m}{n})}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}]"] ["math" "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}[{(3+\\frac{m}{n})}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}]"] ["math" "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}[{(4+\\frac{m}{n})}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980754/state.json" "file_sha256" "17741a48634f24a036a10a6073a4e7584393df9153aec4e24c76bab9abdef2ae"} {"question" "q-49193" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}[{(3+\\frac{2m}{n})}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980754/state.json" "file_sha256" "17741a48634f24a036a10a6073a4e7584393df9153aec4e24c76bab9abdef2ae"} {"question" "q-113880" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is ${\\int }_{0}^{3}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x$ expressed as the limit of a left Riemann sum?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980754/state.json" "file_sha256" "17741a48634f24a036a10a6073a4e7584393df9153aec4e24c76bab9abdef2ae"} {"question" "q-113880" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The definite integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a left Riemann sum as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\n    \n\nwhere $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ and ${x}_{i}=a+iΔx.$\n\nIn the definite integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{3}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nthe function is $f(x)={e}^{x},$ the lower bound is $a=0,$ and the upper bound is $b=3.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{3-0}{n}=\\frac{3}{n},\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[f(0+i\\cdot \\frac{3}{n})\\,\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[f(\\frac{3i}{n})\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{e}^{3i/n}\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980754/state.json" "file_sha256" "17741a48634f24a036a10a6073a4e7584393df9153aec4e24c76bab9abdef2ae"} {"question" "q-113880" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980754/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "523f6f22ecb91e692fe46e7c5d5718162102afd70c6795be6f1a322c4f43120e"} {"question" "q-113880" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980754/state.json" "file_sha256" "17741a48634f24a036a10a6073a4e7584393df9153aec4e24c76bab9abdef2ae"} {"question" "q-113880" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{e}^{3i/n}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3n}]"] ["math" "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{e}^{3i/n}\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}]"] ["math" "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{e}^{3i/n}\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}]"] ["math" "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{e}^{i/n}\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}]"] ["math" "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{e}^{i/n}\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980754/state.json" "file_sha256" "17741a48634f24a036a10a6073a4e7584393df9153aec4e24c76bab9abdef2ae"} {"question" "q-113880" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{e}^{3i/n}\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980754/state.json" "file_sha256" "17741a48634f24a036a10a6073a4e7584393df9153aec4e24c76bab9abdef2ae"} {"question" "q-113884" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is ${\\int }_{1}^{5}{e}^{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x$ expressed as the limit of a left Riemann sum?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980754/state.json" "file_sha256" "17741a48634f24a036a10a6073a4e7584393df9153aec4e24c76bab9abdef2ae"} {"question" "q-113884" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The definite integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a left Riemann sum as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\n    \n\nwhere $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ and ${x}_{i}=a+iΔx.$\n\nIn the definite integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{5}{e}^{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nthe function is $f(x)={e}^{x-1},$ the lower bound is $a=1,$ and the upper bound is $b=5.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{5-1}{n}=\\frac{4}{n},\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{5}{e}^{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[f(1+i\\cdot \\frac{4}{n})\\,\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[f(1+\\frac{4i}{n})\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{e}^{1+4i/n-1}\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{e}^{4i/n}\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980754/state.json" "file_sha256" "17741a48634f24a036a10a6073a4e7584393df9153aec4e24c76bab9abdef2ae"} {"question" "q-113884" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980754/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "523f6f22ecb91e692fe46e7c5d5718162102afd70c6795be6f1a322c4f43120e"} {"question" "q-113884" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980754/state.json" "file_sha256" "17741a48634f24a036a10a6073a4e7584393df9153aec4e24c76bab9abdef2ae"} {"question" "q-113884" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{e}^{4i/n-1}\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}]"] ["math" "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{e}^{4i/n}\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}]"] ["math" "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{e}^{5i/n-1}\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}]"] ["math" "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{e}^{5i/n}\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}]"] ["math" "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{e}^{5i/n}\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980754/state.json" "file_sha256" "17741a48634f24a036a10a6073a4e7584393df9153aec4e24c76bab9abdef2ae"} {"question" "q-113884" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{e}^{4i/n}\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980754/state.json" "file_sha256" "17741a48634f24a036a10a6073a4e7584393df9153aec4e24c76bab9abdef2ae"} {"question" "q-113929" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is ${\\int }_{0}^{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x$ expressed as the limit of a right Riemann sum?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980754/state.json" "file_sha256" "17741a48634f24a036a10a6073a4e7584393df9153aec4e24c76bab9abdef2ae"} {"question" "q-113929" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The definite integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a right Riemann sum as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}f({x}_{k})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{k}=a+kΔx$ and $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$\n\nIn the definite integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nthe function is $f(x)=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x,$ the lower bound is $a=0$ and the upper bound is $b=3.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{3-0}{n}=\\frac{3}{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}f({x}_{k})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[f(0+k\\cdot \\frac{3}{n})\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[f(\\frac{3k}{n})\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{3k}{n})\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980754/state.json" "file_sha256" "17741a48634f24a036a10a6073a4e7584393df9153aec4e24c76bab9abdef2ae"} {"question" "q-113929" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980754/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "523f6f22ecb91e692fe46e7c5d5718162102afd70c6795be6f1a322c4f43120e"} {"question" "q-113929" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980754/state.json" "file_sha256" "17741a48634f24a036a10a6073a4e7584393df9153aec4e24c76bab9abdef2ae"} {"question" "q-113929" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{3k}{n})\\cdot \\frac{1}{3n}]"] ["math" "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{3k}{n})\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}]"] ["math" "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{3k}{n})\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}]"] ["math" "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{k}{3n})\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}]"] ["math" "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{k}{n})\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980754/state.json" "file_sha256" "17741a48634f24a036a10a6073a4e7584393df9153aec4e24c76bab9abdef2ae"} {"question" "q-113929" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{3k}{n})\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980754/state.json" "file_sha256" "17741a48634f24a036a10a6073a4e7584393df9153aec4e24c76bab9abdef2ae"} {"question" "q-346190" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the function $f(x)$ and the value of $b,$ given that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{2}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}[5{(2+\\frac{4k}{n})}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}].\n$$\n\n$\\,f(x)=$\n{{field-1}} $\\,$ and \n$\\,b=$\n{{field-2}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980754/state.json" "file_sha256" "17741a48634f24a036a10a6073a4e7584393df9153aec4e24c76bab9abdef2ae"} {"question" "q-346190" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A definite integral can be defined as the limit of a left Riemann sum as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{k})\\cdot Δx\n$$\n\nwhere $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ and ${x}_{k}=a+kΔx.$\n\nNotice that we're given that the lower limit $a=2.$ \n\nComparing the given summation with the general expression above, we see that $Δx=\\frac{4}{n}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{n}=\\frac{b-2}{n}\\,⟹\\,b=6.\n$$\n\nConsequently, ${x}_{k}=2+\\frac{4k}{n}$ and $f({x}_{k})=5{x}_{k}^{3}.$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{2}^{6}5{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}[5{(2+\\frac{4k}{n})}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \n\n$$\nf(x)=5{x}^{3}\\,\\text{and}\\,b=6.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980754/state.json" "file_sha256" "17741a48634f24a036a10a6073a4e7584393df9153aec4e24c76bab9abdef2ae"} {"question" "q-346190" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980754/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "523f6f22ecb91e692fe46e7c5d5718162102afd70c6795be6f1a322c4f43120e"} {"question" "q-346190" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/